    "title": "fix(anthropic): correct usage accounting, message framing and SSE tolerance",
    "url": "https://github.com/1CatAI/1Cat-vLLM/pull/1440",
    "body": "## Problem\n\nThe `/v1/messages` endpoint has four independent defects on the response path. Grouped in one PR because they interleave in the same functions.\n\n### 1. `input_tokens` reports fresh + cached\n\nvLLM's `prompt_tokens` is the total (OpenAI semantics), but Anthropic reports cache hits separately in `cache_read_input_tokens` and counts only misses in `input_tokens`.\n\nA client that receives neither `cache_read_input_tokens` nor `prompt_tokens_details` has nothing to subtract, so it computes a hit rate of ~48.5% (the signature is `input ≈ 2 × cached`) when the real figure is usually above 99%. It then compacts its context far too early — the user sees their history disappear.\n\nThe first streaming chunk (`message_start`) carries no `prompt_tokens_details` yet. The old code fell back to the total there (437 when the real fresh count was 53). Now it reports 0 and lets `message_delta` supply the accurate value.\n\n### 2. `message_start` omits `type` / `role`\n\nResponses are serialised with `model_dump_json(exclude_unset=True)`, which emits only explicitly assigned fields. Pydantic defaults such as `type: Literal[\"message\"] = \"message\"` and `role: ... = \"assistant\"` are never set, so they are dropped:\n\n```\nexclude_unset=True  -> {\"id\":..., \"content\":[], \"model\":..., \"usage\":...}\nexclude_unset=False -> {\"id\":..., \"type\":\"message\", \"role\":\"assistant\", ...}\n```\n\nThe Anthropic SDK treats a message without `type`/`role` as unparseable and **silently discards it**. After a reload, every assistant message disappears from the client's history while the tool-call state survives.\n\n### 3. Upstream error frame becomes a 500\n\nThe upstream chat stream can interleave `{\"error\": {...}}` (a tool parser exception, for instance). Feeding that to `ChatCompletionStreamResponse.model_validate_json` raises `ValidationError: model/choices Field required`, turning a readable upstream error into a 500 for the whole turn — and the tool-call result is lost. Now detected and emitted as an Anthropic `error` event.\n\n### 4. Non-`data:` SSE frames treated as errors\n\nComment lines, blank lines and `event:` / `id:` / `retry:` fields are legal SSE. The old code answered them with `error: Invalid data format`; clients abort the turn on an error, so tool calls are not executed and the body is never delivered. Long-running turns always hit a comment frame, so this fired routinely. Now skipped.\n\n## Additions\n\n- Opt-in `token_ids` / `prompt_token_ids` passthrough, mirroring the OpenAI protocol's `return_token_ids`, for clients that meter tokens per chunk.\n- `VLLM_DEBUG_ANTHROPIC_TRACE` (off by default): logs a structural summary and dumps the last complete request for offline replay. Structure and lengths only, never content.\n- HEAD probes on `/v1/messages`, so a readiness check pointed at the Anthropic route does not get 405 and mark the instance dead.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Streaming behind a proxy: hit rate reads correctly, history survives reloads.\n- Tool-parser exception mid-stream: client receives a parseable error event, not a 500.",
